PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1768760743
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CRemembering the 1993 refresh
OL,4,Cof BBC One news branding
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt seems astonishing now that the main
OL,7,FBBC One programmes lost all but the
OL,8,Fmost subtle hints of a common identity
OL,9,Fin the mid-1980s.
OL,11,FThis had long been the practice on ITV
OL,12,Fwhere each news bulletin had been seen
OL,13,Fas a programme in its own right ` News
OL,14,Fat One had a very different feel to
OL,15,FNews at 545 which in turn was quite
OL,16,Funlike News at Ten. The common link was
OL,17,FITN. But the look of the news service
OL,18,Fwas not of any corporate importance to
OL,19,Findividual ITV companies or the network
OL,20,Fitself.
OL,23,APub: 16-Apr-2023Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13803
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1768760743
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CRemembering the 1993 refresh
OL,4,Cof BBC One news branding
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut why was this ever the case with the
OL,7,FBBC? An organisation with news at its
OL,8,Fvery centre.
OL,10,FThe 1981 revamp gave each of the three
OL,11,Fdaily programmes distinct personalities
OL,12,Fbut they still shared a common visual
OL,13,Fidentity.
OL,15,FThis broke down in the mid-80s. First
OL,16,Fthe new Six O'Clock News, then the Nine
OL,17,Fand finally the relaunched One had
OL,18,Ftheir own signature tunes, titles,
OL,19,Fgraphics and sets.
OL,23,APub: 16-Apr-2023Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13804
SC,0004
